   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     93,
     101
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests for {@link Symmetry010Chronology} and its companion {@link Symmetry010Date}. <p> The Symmetry010 calendar keeps every month at 30 days except the middle month of each quarter (February, May, August, November), which has 31 days. A leap year appends a \"leap week\", so its December stretches from the usual 30 days to 37 days. These tests exercise construction, conversion to/from the ISO calendar, field access, arithmetic and formatting against that structure."
   },
